- CRM business logic
- CRM triggers
- CRM workflows

------------------------------------------------

Architecture Rules

Business modules define WHAT exists.

Platform defines HOW it executes.

Execution never belongs inside business modules.

Business logic must exist only once.

Never duplicate:

- business rules
- lifecycle logic
- ownership
- state transitions
- triggers
- workflows
- domain functions

------------------------------------------------

# Domain Evolution

Migration numbers are NOT the SSOT.

Domains are the SSOT.

Business modules may evolve through multiple migrations.

Example:

003_devices_rev19.sql

024_devices_extensions_rev19.sql

041_devices_automation_rev20.sql

All belong to the same Device Engine.

Immutable migrations NEVER justify placing business logic into another module.

If a new Device function is required:

Create a new Device migration.

NOT an Edge migration.

------------------------------------------------

# Edge Layer

Edge is an API layer only.

Edge may contain:

- RPC wrappers
- authentication guards
- authorization helpers
- tenant validation
- request validation
- response helpers
- logging helpers
- API utilities

Edge must NEVER contain:

- business logic
- triggers
- workflows
- lifecycle management
- state transitions
- device logic
- booking logic
- CRM logic
- logistics logic
- commerce logic

Edge calls business modules.

Business modules never belong to Edge.

------------------------------------------------

If ownership is unclear:

STOP

Explain which module owns the SSOT.

Never invent a second owner.